    "summary": "Double portrait of an Indian on the left facing a Turk on the right; single-page painting on an album folio. Indian wears a long dress over pants, with a daggar and two swords (long and short) tucked into the sash tied around his waist. In one hand he holds a piece of food close to his mouth. Opposite, the Turk wears a long coat over his shoulders, covering his long dress and pants.  In his hand he holds a slender pipe. Inscribed. Album contains 44 paintings and drawings, mostly of Persian costumes and animals with some drawings by Kaempfer.\r\nInk and opaque watercolour on paper. Album is bound in brown leather with gold gilt  decoration. Inside covers have marbled paper.",
